  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Mass of an electron $=9.108 \\times 10^{-31} \\mathrm{kg}$\r\nMass of one mole of electron\r\n$$\r\n=\\left(9.108 \\times 10^{-31} \\times 6.023 \\times 10^{23}\\right) \\mathrm{kg}\r\n$$\r\nThen, number of mole of electron in $1 \\mathrm{kg}$\r\n$$\r\n\\begin{array}{l}\r\n=\\frac{1}{9.108 \\times 6.023 \\times 10^{-8}} \\\\\r\n=\\frac{1}{9.108 \\times 6.023} \\times 10^{8} \\text { mole of } e^{-}\r\n\\end{array}\r\n$$",
